Subject: [PATCH 13/13] fix: wire continuous-learning enforcement chain
 end-to-end
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Before: observational only — observations captured but analysis was
commented out, no instinct reload, no context injection, no enforcement.

After:
- triggerBackgroundAnalysis() runs analyzeObservations after every 20
  observations (was commented out at observer.ts:330)
- reloadActiveInstincts() loads project + global active instincts into
  cache at session_start
- context event handler prepends <learned-rules> developer message
  containing all active instincts before every model invocation
- buildEnforcementBlock() formats instincts as mandatory rules with
  trigger/action pairs
- 3 regression tests proving: pattern detection creates instincts,
  instincts persist across storage instances, enforcement text is
  structured correctly

Chain: observation → auto-analysis → instinct storage → session reload →
context injection → model sees enforcement rules
